  concept: "Authored objective: Trip during a sustained jam.\nAuthored requirement:
    Recorded from the solved timer voltage and motor state during the jam test. voltage
    \u2265 4.8 V. voltage \u2264 5.2 V.\nGeneral teaching principle: Protection logic
    must be verified under both normal and fault conditions, including reset and
    recovery behavior.\nOnly fresh, authoritative game evidence can establish that
    this objective is complete."
  analogy: A safety lock must prevent unintended activation even when the normal
    switch would permit it.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: Passing a normal-operation test is not proof that the protection
    system responds correctly to faults.
